# Line-ending policy.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: this repo is edited from both Windows tools and WSL. Without a
# policy, a Windows-side editor rewrites whole files to CRLF, producing phantom
# diffs where every line shows as changed but the content is byte-identical
# (observed: all 13 .kiro/agents/*.md files, plus .kiro/skills/*/SKILL.md and
# scripts/run-tests.sh). Beyond the noise, CRLF actively breaks two things here:
#   1. Agent/skill frontmatter — parsers that match a bare `---` fence line see
#      `---\r` and can reject the whole block, which silently strips an agent's
#      declared `tools:` grant.
#   2. Shell scripts — `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` fails to exec on Linux.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes to LF in the index and checks out LF in the
# working tree on every platform. Scoped to the file types we actually author
# rather than `*` so no binary or vendored asset gets renormalized by surprise.

*.md    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.cfg   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
Dockerfile     text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary
